{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 51, :comments ["<b>Six hundred thousand and one thousand seven hundred and thirty.</b> Know that this number, and likewise the one at Sinai which came to six hundred thousand and three thousand five hundred and fifty, did not include all Israel, for they have no end or limit, and we do not know from this the total number of all Israel — for Israel were not counted here or there except from twenty years old and upward, all who go forth to war in Israel. And surely there were among Israel those (who are from twenty years old and downward) and those who are from twenty years old and upward — many elders, and many sick and feeble — who are not included in the count because they were not fit for the army and are not among those who go forth to war. If so, the number of the children of Israel is not mentioned anywhere in the Scriptures, and we do not know it at all. For from the time they went down to Egypt with seventy souls, the blessing spread among them until they grew to sixty myriad who went out from there, the males alone apart from the little ones, and they are the very ones who received the Torah in the third month after their exodus. And the blessing spread among them further in the second month in the second year after their exodus from the land of Egypt, when they grew to sixty myriad from twenty years old and upward, all who go forth to war." "<b>And we learn</b> from this that at Mount Sinai when they received the Torah they had a known number, and within a short time — about ten months from the giving of the Torah until they were counted in the wilderness of Sinai — their number rose beyond limit. And the truth is that Israel are not within the category of counting at all, and their number was never known in any of the generations, nor was their count investigated with precision at any time. For who can count what defies counting and has no number? Behold, they are under the promise (Genesis 32:13): ״ושמתי את זרעך כחול הים אשר לא יספר מרוב״, and thus the Holy One, blessed be He, said to Abraham (ibid. 15:5): ״וספור הכוכבים״, and promised him and said: ״כה יהיה זרעך״. And likewise we find that Moses said to them in the fortieth year (Deuteronomy 1:10): ״והנכם היום ככוכבי השמים לרוב״. Also Balaam, our adversary, testified concerning us and said: ״מי מנה עפר יעקב ומספר את רובע ישראל״. And we find concerning David, peace be upon him, when he commanded Joab to count them, that they came to one million and three hundred thousand sword-bearing men, as it is written (II Samuel 24:9): ״ויתן יואב את מספר מפקד העם אל המלך ותהי ישראל שמונה מאות אלף איש חיל שולף חרב ואיש יהודה חמש מאות אלף״. And it is known that if mighty men, sword-bearers, came to this enormous figure, there is no doubt that there is no end or limit to the number of the masses and the poor of the people and the youths and the elders — and reason attests to this, and the Scriptures prove it likewise, for they are a clearer testimony than reason itself. And thus we find regarding the future, that Isaiah the prophet, peace be upon him, promised us that Israel shall be in the multiplication of the people, an immense multitude more than all the nations of the world, as he said (Isaiah 54:1): ״כי רבים בני שוממה מבני בעולה אמר ה׳״ — and that they shall gather from the four corners of the earth in a very great multitude, as he said (ibid. 49:12): ״הנה אלה מרחוק יבאו והנה אלה מצפון ומים ואלה מארץ סינים״, and you shall say in your heart: ״מי ילד לי את אלה ואני שכולה וגלמודה גולה וסורה ואלה מי גדל הן אני נשארתי לבדי אלה איפה הם״. The prophet, peace be upon him, mentioned the word אלה three times, to allude that the Shekhinah — which is comprised of six extremities — shall return with them, for correspondingly David mentioned it six times שמירה in the psalm."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {1 "The verse citations in parentheses for Genesis and the II Samuel reference appear to be editorial glosses; Genesis 15:5 and 32:13 and II Samuel 24:9 are the correct sources for the quoted verses. The closing Kabbalistic allusion to 'six extremities' and 'six times שמירה' (referring to Psalm 12) is rendered literally without expansion."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:36:30.295084227Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}